WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.980
This slash. Do I have to buy both coins?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:14.721
No. It means bitcoin is priced in USDT. When you buy, you pay USDT and get bitcoin.

00:00:14.721 --> 00:00:17.160
When you sell, it goes the other way.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.215
We practise with a virtual account. Make sure it's spot, not futures.

00:00:39.215 --> 00:00:43.122
Pick the pair, choose Buy, then enter the amount. Before you submit,

00:00:43.122 --> 00:00:47.030
check whether the box wants an amount of money or a number of coins.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:12.975
Say the fill price is 50,000 and you spend 100. You get 0. 002 bitcoin.

00:01:12.975 --> 00:01:19.668
Now assume a 0. 1% fee taken separately from your USDT. You spend 100. 10 in total.

00:01:19.668 --> 00:01:22.410
Real rules depend on the platform.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.770
So once I tap Buy, I definitely have the coins?

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:40.691
Check the trade history too.

00:01:40.691 --> 00:01:43.992
Not filled, partly filled and fully filled are different.

00:01:43.992 --> 00:01:46.830
Check the real average price and the fee as well.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.971
Your first practice isn't about guessing up or down.

00:01:58.971 --> 00:02:00.959
It's about checking these five things.

00:02:00.959 --> 00:02:04.150
And when you're done, it's fine to not make a real trade yet.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:15.820
When you're ready for a real first trade, open Bitget through our partner link.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.390
Code nexu888 gets part of your trading fees back. Same five checks, every time.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:25.527
Say the price rises and you sell. So why is your bank balance still the same?

00:02:25.527 --> 00:02:26.300
Next episode.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.820
Understand first, then act.
